        register කළාම, SW එක install වෙනවා ඒත් එම load එකේදීම page එක
        control කරන්නේ නෑ (SW spec එකේම standard behavior එකක් —
        පළමු register වෙන SW එක current page එක control කරන්නේ නෑ,
        ඊළඟ navigation එකේදී විතරයි). ඒ නිසා Home page එකේ පළමු visit
        එකේදී Chrome ට low-confidence, simple dialog එකක් පෙන්නන්න
        සිද්ධ වුනා. Blog post එකට navigate කරනකොට (2 වෙනි navigation),
        SW එක දැනටමත් "controlling" state එකේ තියෙන නිසා richer dialog
        එක පෙන්නුවා.

        ✅ PERMANENT FIX: Registration script එක <head> එකට, ඉතාම
        ඉක්මනින්ම (blocking network request එකක් නොවන "register()"
        call එකක්, main content render එකට කිසිම බලපෑමක් නැති
        async/non-blocking call එකක්) දාලා, "load" event එකට කලින්ම
        trigger කරනවා. මෙය Chrome ට SW එක install+active වෙන්න
        හැකි තරම් ඉක්මනින්ම ලැබෙන chance එක වැඩි කරනවා, page load
        එකේම (හෝ ඊළඟ ඉක්මන් reload එකකදී) richer dialog එකට
        eligible වෙන්න පුළුවන් වෙනවා — Home page එකද, Post page
        එකද කියලා වෙනසක් නැතුව site එක පුරාම consistent PWA install
        experience එකක් සහතික කරනවා.

        🎯 2026-08 FIX (Duplicate Registration Call + Confusing
        Console Warnings — Google Search Console URL Inspection tool
        flagged 2 identical "SW registration failed" warnings on a
        single test): ROOT CAUSE was that doRegister() was called
        directly below AND attached as an "astro:page-load" listener
        — but Astro's ClientRouter dispatches "astro:page-load" once
        on the VERY FIRST page load too (not only on later client-side
        SPA navigations). That meant register() actually ran TWICE for
        the same initial load, producing two duplicate registration
        attempts and, when registration fails (e.g. inside sandboxed
        tools like Google Search Console's URL Inspection, which does
        not support Service Workers at all), two duplicate console
        warnings. A "hasRegistered" guard flag now ensures doRegister()
        only performs an actual register() call once per real
        page/navigation - the immediate call runs first, and the
        "astro:page-load" listener is now a no-op on that same initial
        load (guard already tripped), only doing real work on genuine
        subsequent SPA navigations. If a registration attempt fails,
        the guard is deliberately reset so a later real navigation can
        still retry - this preserves the exact same retry-resilience
        behavior as before, just without the duplicate first-load call.

        🛡️ SELF-HEALING GUARDS (retained):
        - "serviceWorker" API නොමැති browsers වල silently skip වෙනවා.
        - hasRegistered guard flag එකෙන් View Transitions (ClientRouter)
          client-side navigation වලදීත් duplicate registration
          attempts (initial load එකේදී විශේෂයෙන්) වළක්වයි.
        - registration fail උනොත් (offline, unsupported browser
          edge-case ආදී) silently log කරලා core site functionality
          කිසිවකට බලපෑමක් නැතුව ඉදිරියට යනවා, සහ guard flag එක reset
          කරලා ඊළඟ real navigation එකකදී retry කරන්න ඉඩ දෙනවා.
       ========================================================== */}
    <script is:inline>
      (function registerServiceWorkerEarly() {
        if (!("serviceWorker" in navigator)) return;

        let hasRegistered = false;

        function doRegister() {
          // Duplicate-call guard: Astro's ClientRouter dispatches
          // "astro:page-load" once on the initial page load too (not
          // just subsequent SPA navigations). Without this guard,
          // register() would run twice on the very first load - once
          // from the direct call below, once via the listener -
          // producing duplicate registration attempts and duplicate
          // console warnings when registration fails (e.g. in
          // sandboxed test tools like Google Search Console's URL
          // Inspection, which does not support Service Workers at
          // all).
          if (hasRegistered) return;
          hasRegistered = true;

          navigator.serviceWorker
            .register("/sw.js")
            .then((registration) => {
              console.log("SW registered (early):", registration.scope);
            })
            .catch((err) => {
              console.warn("SW registration failed:", err);
              // Reset the guard on failure so a later real navigation
              // can still retry registration (preserves the original
              // retry-resilience behavior).
              hasRegistered = false;
            });
        }

        // 🎯 ASAP TRIGGER: "load" event එකට කලින්ම, script tag එක
        // parse වෙන ගමන්ම register() call කරනවා. register() call එක
        // itself non-blocking (Promise-based) නිසා, main content
        // render/paint එකට කිසිම delay එකක් හෝ blocking side-effect
        // එකක් ඇති නොකරයි — Network Information API/Fetch handler
        // setup එක background thread එකක (Service Worker thread)
        // සිදු වෙනවා.
        doRegister();

        // 🎯 View Transitions (ClientRouter) client-side navigation
        // සඳහාත් register logic එකම attach කරනවා — hasRegistered
        // guard එක නිසා මෙය initial load එකේදී no-op එකක් වේ (already
        // registered above), නමුත් ඊළඟ genuine SPA navigation එකකදී
        // (හෝ පළමු attempt එක fail වුනොත් retry එකක් ලෙස) working
        // logic එකක් ලෙස පවතී.
        document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", doRegister);
      })();
    </script>

    {/* ==========================================================
        🎯 NEW: CORE WEB VITALS MONITORING (SEO Enhancement Pass #2)

        WHY: Core Web Vitals (LCP, CLS, INP) are a confirmed Google
        ranking factor. Without any client-side measurement, there is
        no visibility into real-user performance regressions — issues
        only surface reactively via PageSpeed Insights manual checks.

        WHAT THIS DOES: Uses the browser's native PerformanceObserver
        API (zero external dependencies, zero extra HTTP requests,
        ~15 lines of vanilla JS) to capture LCP, CLS, and INP as they
        occur, then logs them to the console in development and
        (if Google Tag Manager is enabled per config.json) pushes them
        into the existing dataLayer so they surface in GA4/GTM
        reports the site may already have configured — reusing the
        SAME gtm.dataLayer array that astro-gtm-lite (already an
        active dependency, see astro.config.mjs) creates, rather than
        introducing a second, competing analytics mechanism.

        SAFE-BY-DEFAULT: if config.google_tag_manager.enable is false
        (the current default in config.json), this script simply
        console.logs the metrics locally and does nothing else —
        zero network calls, zero external services contacted, fully
        inert on production until GTM is turned on.

        PERFORMANCE: this script is deferred (`is:inline` + attached
        after the "load" event fires, not before) so it can never
        compete with or delay LCP/FCP itself — instrumentation code
        must never be the thing that harms the metrics it measures.

        🎯 2026-08 FIX (Misleading CLS Console Display — Google Search
        Console URL Inspection tool logged "[Web Vitals] CLS: 4",
        which reads as an alarmingly high score even though the real
        underlying CLS was an excellent 0.004): ROOT CAUSE was that
        the console-logged "value" for CLS was always the *1000-scaled
        integer (the same value intentionally used for the GA4/GTM
        dataLayer push, matching that platform's existing numeric
        convention), so a genuinely great CLS of 0.004 displayed as a
        bare "4" with no decimal/scale context in the console log
        text itself. FIX: the human-readable console log now shows
        CLS with real decimal precision (e.g. "0.004") while the
        GA4/GTM dataLayer push keeps the exact same scaled-integer
        value as before (zero change to any existing analytics/report
        pipeline depending on that convention) - display and analytics
        values are now computed and used separately.
       ========================================================== */}
    <script is:inline define:vars={{ gtmEnabled: config.google_tag_manager.enable }}>
      (function initWebVitalsMonitoring() {
        if (typeof PerformanceObserver === "undefined") return;

        function reportMetric(name, value, extra) {
          // Display value: CLS is a small decimal (e.g. 0.004-0.1) and
          // is now shown with real decimals instead of a scaled
          // integer, since "CLS: 4" (meaning 0.004 after *1000
          // scaling) reads as an alarming score when reviewed in
          // tools like Google Search Console's console log viewer,
          // even though it represents an excellent (near-zero) score.
          const displayValue = name === "CLS" ? value.toFixed(3) : Math.round(value);
          // Analytics value: kept as the scaled integer (CLS * 1000)
          // for GA4/GTM dataLayer push, matching the existing/standard
          // convention already used by this integration - unchanged.
          const analyticsValue = Math.round(name === "CLS" ? value * 1000 : value);

          console.log(`[Web Vitals] ${name}:`, displayValue, extra || "");
          if (gtmEnabled && window.dataLayer) {
            window.dataLayer.push({
              event: "web_vitals",
              metric_name: name,
              metric_value: analyticsValue,
            });
          }
        }

        window.addEventListener("load", function () {
          try {
            // Largest Contentful Paint
            new PerformanceObserver((list) => {
              const entries = list.getEntries();
              const last = entries[entries.length - 1];
              if (last) reportMetric("LCP", last.renderTime || last.loadTime || last.startTime);
            }).observe({ type: "largest-contentful-paint", buffered: true });

            // Cumulative Layout Shift
            let clsValue = 0;
            new PerformanceObserver((list) => {
              for (const entry of list.getEntries()) {
                if (!entry.hadRecentInput) clsValue += entry.value;
              }
              reportMetric("CLS", clsValue);
            }).observe({ type: "layout-shift", buffered: true });

            // Interaction to Next Paint (event timing)
            new PerformanceObserver((list) => {
              for (const entry of list.getEntries()) {
                if (entry.duration) reportMetric("INP", entry.duration, entry.name);
              }
            }).observe({ type: "event", buffered: true, durationThreshold: 40 });
          } catch (err) {
            // Older browsers without support for these entry types —
            // fail silently, core site functionality unaffected.
            console.warn("Web Vitals monitoring unavailable:", err);
          }
        });
      })();
    </script>

    {/* ==========================================================
        🛡️ CONTENT PROTECTION — ANTI-SCRAPING BEHAVIOR LAYER
        (Smooth Selection Restriction + Friendly Centered Notice)

        WHAT THIS DOES:
        - Blocks the default browser "copy" action (Ctrl+C, right-click
          → Copy, long-press → Copy on mobile) anywhere OUTSIDE form
          fields, and shows a short, friendly, auto-fading CENTERED
          card notice instead of a jarring native alert() or a
          bottom-pinned strip of text.
        - Blocks the native right-click context menu outside form
          fields (the #1 easy vector casual scrapers/visitors use to
          "Save As" or "Inspect → Copy").
        - Blocks dragging images out of the page (another easy-copy
          vector for images).
        - selectstart is prevented as a defensive fallback for older
          mobile WebViews that don't fully respect the CSS
          user-select:none rule declared above.

        WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO (by design):
        - Does NOT touch input/textarea/select/contenteditable targets
          — Contact form, Comment box, and Search bar remain 100%
          normal (typing, native text selection/copy/paste all work).
        - Does NOT attempt to block browser DevTools or "View Page
          Source" — this is technically impossible to reliably block,
          and real scraping bots fetch raw HTML via HTTP directly
          (never through a rendered browser+mouse), so blocking
          DevTools would add user friction for zero actual anti-scrape
          benefit. This layer targets the casual "select-and-copy"
          human workflow, not automated bot fetching (robots.txt /
          IndexNow / crawler rules already govern that layer).
        - Does NOT run more than once per short window — a 2.2s
          throttle prevents the notice from spamming if a person
          repeatedly right-clicks/tries to copy.

        SELF-HEALING: the notice element is created on-demand via
        JavaScript (not a static DOM node), so it can never end up in
        a broken/missing state across Astro View Transitions
        (ClientRouter) page swaps — every time it's needed, if it
        isn't already in the live DOM, it's freshly created and
        appended to <body>.

        Listeners are registered once at document level (delegation),
        which persists for the full SPA session regardless of
        ClientRouter page swaps — no re-registration/cleanup needed,
        since these are not tied to any specific page's DOM nodes.

        2026-08 REDESIGN: the notice moved from a small bottom-fixed
        pill to a centered, rounded modal-style card (see the
        #content-protection-toast CSS rules above, in the earlier
        <style> block). The DOM structure built here now includes a
        dedicated icon wrapper (cp-icon-wrap, holding a lock SVG)
        instead of the old small colored dot — everything else about
        the throttle/timing/targeting logic is unchanged.
       ========================================================== */}
    <script is:inline>
      (function initContentProtection() {
        let lastNoticeAt = 0;
        const NOTICE_THROTTLE_MS = 2200;
        const NOTICE_VISIBLE_MS = 2600;
        const NOTICE_MESSAGE = "මෙම අන්තර්ගතය පිටපත් කිරීම වළක්වා ඇත";

        function isEditableTarget(target) {
          if (!target || !target.tagName) return false;
          const tag = target.tagName.toLowerCase();
          if (tag === "input" || tag === "textarea" || tag === "select" || tag === "option") return true;
          if (target.isContentEditable) return true;
          // Allow selection inside any element explicitly opted back in
          if (target.closest && target.closest("[data-allow-select]")) return true;
          return false;
        }

        function buildLockIconSvg() {
          // width/height set directly on the <svg> tag (not only via
          // CSS) as a defensive belt-and-suspenders measure — this
          // guarantees a correctly-sized 17x17 icon even in the
          // unlikely event the stylesheet hasn't parsed yet at the
          // exact instant this element is inserted.
          return (
            '<svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" ' +
            'stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">' +
            '<rect x="4" y="10.5" width="16" height="9.5" rx="2.2"></rect>' +
            '<path d="M7.5 10.5V7.2a4.5 4.5 0 019 0v3.3"></path>' +
            '<circle cx="12" cy="14.7" r="1.4" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"></circle>' +
            "</svg>"
          );
        }

        function showProtectionNotice() {
          const now = Date.now();
          if (now - lastNoticeAt < NOTICE_THROTTLE_MS) return;
          lastNoticeAt = now;

          let toast = document.getElementById("content-protection-toast");
          if (!toast) {
            toast = document.createElement("div");
            toast.id = "content-protection-toast";
            toast.setAttribute("role", "status");
            toast.setAttribute("aria-live", "polite");

            const iconWrap = document.createElement("span");
            iconWrap.className = "cp-icon-wrap";
            iconWrap.setAttribute("aria-hidden", "true");
            iconWrap.innerHTML = buildLockIconSvg();

            const text = document.createElement("span");
            text.className = "cp-text";

            toast.appendChild(iconWrap);
            toast.appendChild(text);
            document.body.appendChild(toast);
          }

          const textEl = toast.querySelector(".cp-text");
          if (textEl) textEl.textContent = NOTICE_MESSAGE;

          toast.classList.add("show");
          clearTimeout(toast._cpHideTimer);
          toast._cpHideTimer = setTimeout(() => {
            toast.classList.remove("show");
          }, NOTICE_VISIBLE_MS);
        }

        // Right-click / long-press context menu — main "Save As / Copy"
        // vector outside form fields.
        document.addEventListener("contextmenu", function (e) {
          if (isEditableTarget(e.target)) return;
          e.preventDefault();
          showProtectionNotice();
        });

        // Ctrl+C / Cmd+C / right-click → Copy — all funnel through the
        // native "copy" event regardless of trigger method.
        document.addEventListener("copy", function (e) {
          if (isEditableTarget(e.target)) return;
          e.preventDefault();
          showProtectionNotice();
        });

        // Cut is meaningless outside editable fields, block silently
        // (no notice spam needed — copy/contextmenu already inform).
        document.addEventListener("cut", function (e) {
          if (isEditableTarget(e.target)) return;
          e.preventDefault();
        });

        // Defensive fallback for browsers/WebViews that don't fully
        // respect the CSS user-select:none rule declared above.
        document.addEventListener("selectstart", function (e) {
          if (isEditableTarget(e.target)) return;
          e.preventDefault();
        });

        // Prevent dragging images out of the page (easy image-scrape
        // vector). Scoped to <img> only — does not affect FeaturedSlider
        // touch-swipe logic (that uses touchstart/touchend, not drag).
        document.addEventListener("dragstart", function (e) {
          const target = e.target;
          if (target && target.tagName && target.tagName.toLowerCase() === "img") {
            e.preventDefault();
          }
        });
      })();
    </script>

    <ClientRouter fallback="swap" />
  </head>

  <body class="bg-[#050505] text-[#f8fafc] min-h-screen flex flex-col antialiased selection:bg-emerald-500/30 selection:text-[#34d399] overflow-x-hidden" style="touch-action: pan-y; overscroll-behavior-x: none;">
    <TwSizeIndicator />
    <Header />
    <main id="main-content" class="min-h-[60vh] flex-1 bg-[#050505]">
      <slot />
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
